    "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/construction-project-coordinator-topeka-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Construction Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Construction Project Coordinator - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Construction Project Coordinator Facilities Services Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Construction Project Coordinator Facilities Services Staff Full-time Position Title: Construction Project Coordinator Department: Facilities Services Advertised Pay: Lower $70,000's Campus Location: Washburn University ApplicationReview: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: Primary responsibilities are to assist with the organization of the operations of construction on Washburn campuses by assisting with the coordination of resources and equipment for construction projects, with the goal of getting them completed accurately, on time, and within budget. Projects may range from new construction or renovations to program specific equipment installations. This position may be asked to help with concept development, design, planning, bidding, and/or implementation processes. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Essential Functions: • Support staff with project management throughout the construction process for new construction, major renovations, and/or alterations to campus facilities to ensure the University's expectations and requirements are met. • Work with architectural and engineering firms along with staff and other University stakeholders during all phases of construction to verify the project is reflective of the design/construction plans. • May serve as a liaison among campus departments and external contractors for coordinating and scheduling projects. • Assist with monitoring construction sites to ensure projects have necessary resources, are completed on time, and within budget. • Inspect projects, drawings, and documents to ensure compliance with specifications and standards. • Assist with the studies and observations of the physical needs of Washburn campuses and coordinate the necessary repairs, renovations, and/or alterations to Washburn facilities. • Support staff in management of project timelines to report and adjust for delays and emergencies as they arise. • Facilitate acquisition of needed materials, tools, and equipment. • Ensure appropriate permits are obtained and filed. • Assist with monitoring project costs. • Work with contractors to address issues that arise during construction. With assistance from staff, identify acceptable approaches to resolve issues within time and cost constraints. • Continually update project files (as-built drawings, test reports, O&M manuals, cost data, insurance documents and warranties) for reporting and project management. • Assist with maintenance of university records (project records, shop drawings, original equipment manufacturer manuals, etc.) using department software. Collaborate with staff to complete paperwork (budgets, cost estimates, upkeep, etc.), including project closeout process. • Provide assistance with project research and resolution. • Support staff in the preparation of reports, collecting and formulating data. Work collaboratively to assist with the preparation of the budget for yearly capital improvement requests. • Assist staff with updating floor plans and campus and utility maps. • May attend meetings to provide assistance to other units within the department, or to represent the department throughout campus. • Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Non-Essential Functions: • Coordinates furniture selection for departments. Required Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree in engineering, architecture, architectural engineering, or construction management. • Previous construction experience required. • Demonstrated effective interpersonal skills. • Valid driver’s license with a driving record that meets Washburn standards. Physical Requirements: • Ability to work from a ladder or lift, tour the campus, buildings, and job sites, which may include uneven surfaces and/or stairs. Preferred Qualifications: • Two years of construction project management experience. • Knowledge in Revit or Auto CAD. • Experience with ADA, building, and life safety codes. • Proficient MS Office Suite skills. • Proven ability to handle multiple projects with evidence of completion within established budget and timelines. Exempt, Full-time Background check and driving history are required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 75f28f41 Last Name (required) 51b3f441 Email (required) 06393d78 Job Alert ac296d7a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Services Facilities Services Categories Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am – 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University’s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 8955f7c0 Last Name (required) f4ecd927 Email (required) e5192c90 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking “I Accept” or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"
