    "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/maintenance-technician-four-positions-updated-7-7-20026-topeka-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician (Four Positions) (Updated 7/7/20026)",
      "description": "Maintenance Technician (Four Positions) (Updated 7/7/20026) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Maintenance Technician (Four Positions) (Updated 7/7/20026) Facilities Services Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Maintenance Technician (Four Positions) (Updated 7/7/20026) Facilities Services Staff Full-time Position Title: Maintenance Technician (Four Positions) (Updated 7/7/20026) Department: Facilities Services (CBU) Advertised Pay: $20.60/hr Campus Location: Washburn University Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: Under general supervision, the Maintenance Technician performs a variety of skilled and semi-skilled duties to ensure the proper functioning, safety, and operational efficiency of Washburn buildings, systems, and equipment. This role requires a proactive approach to maintenance, strong problem-solving skills, and collaboration with campus staff, contractors, and external partners. The Maintenance Technician is a vital member of the Facilities team, contributing to a well-maintained and safe environment for the entire Washburn community. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Essential Functions: HVAC, Boiler, and Mechanical Systems • Operate, monitor, and perform preventative and corrective maintenance on heating, ventilation, air conditioning (HVAC), and boiler systems. This includes tasks such as repairing boilers, pumps, and related support equipment, and checking building automation systems (BAS) for temperature and equipment functionality. General Building and System Maintenance • Perform skilled and semi-skilled repair work on building structures and mechanical systems as assigned through the Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS) or other software. • Inspect and address deficiencies in building systems, including plumbing, electrical, and HVAC equipment. • Maintain building interiors by repairing ceiling tiles, floor tile, cove bases, and other materials; patching and painting interior walls and surfaces; and replacing lamps. • Address plumbing issues, including clearing sewage blockages, drain lines, and cleaning roof drains. • Conduct repairs on doors, locks, and other hardware. Inspections and Diagnostics • Inspect and test various campus systems and equipment, including air compressors, fire sprinkler piping systems, grease traps, and sewer pumps, to ensure optimal function and safety. Facility Operations and Support • Provide essential service and event support across campus as directed by Facilities supervisors. • Perform snow and ice removal duties as assigned during inclement weather. • Conduct maintenance on water features, swimming pools, and/or whirlpools, including minor water chemical treatments, adhering to manufacturer guidelines and Washburn standards. Compliance and Reporting • Ensure all maintenance tasks are performed according to manufacturer specifications and Washburn, local, and OSHA safety regulations. • Document all completed repairs, work orders, and inspections accurately within the CMMS or other designated software. • Communicate deficiencies to immediate supervisors and recommend process improvements to enhance operational efficiency. Collaboration • Work with and assist engineers, contractors, and consultants during safety evaluations, system repairs, and project planning. Provide information on Washburn procedures and practices to support project coordination. Professional Conduct • Always maintain a professional, safe, and clean work environment. Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: • High school diploma, GED, or equivalent. • One year of relevant work experience in building maintenance, or completion of a certified trade program in a related field. • Demonstrated training in Building Maintenance, acquired through on-the-job training or a completed certification program. • Proven ability in maintaining commercial building mechanical systems. • Effective communication skills. • Demonstrated ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. • Demonstrated effective troubleshooting and problem-solving skills to diagnose and repair issues efficiently. • Valid driver’s license with an acceptable driving record under Washburn standards. Physical Requirements: • The ability to move, lift, and maneuver materials weighing up to 50 pounds. Heavier items may require team lifting. • Ability to work from a ladder and/or lifts, safely. Training provided. • Must be able to respond to emergency service calls outside of regularly scheduled work hours and be available to work various shifts as assigned. • The role involves exposure to various physical hazards associated with building maintenance and repair, as well as outdoor weather conditions. • This is a Designated Safety Sensitive position and will be required to undergo drug screening. Preferred Qualifications: • Proven expertise in at least two different skilled trades relevant to building maintenance (e.g., electrical, plumbing, carpentry). • Experience with a Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS). • Experience with a Building Automation System (BAS). • Safety or chemical management training. • Fundamental computer literacy, including the ability to enter data and communicate via email. Special Instructions to Applicants: Hourly, Full-time, Mon-Fri, 8am-4:30pm Background check, driving history, and drug screen are required. Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) fe13c01a Last Name (required) ebae2528 Email (required) daacfa53 Job Alert 8647cd68 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Services Facilities Services Categories Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am – 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University’s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) d7120e22 Last Name (required) c4819846 Email (required) 92b2286b Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking “I Accept” or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"
