    "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/office-coordinator-topeka-kansas-united-states-4cbd4189-a31c-4067-99fb-0cd2b6877113": {
      "title": "Office Coordinator",
      "description": "Office Coordinator - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Office Coordinator Human Resources Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Office Coordinator Human Resources Staff Full-time Position Title: Office Coordinator Department: Human Resources Advertised Pay: Base $18.54/hour with potential for a higher entry rate commensurate with experience Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: This position is responsible for providing administrative support and coordination for Human Resources and is responsible for delivering prompt, accurate, and exemplary customer service to administrators, faculty, staff, students, applicants, and external constituents through multiple methods of communication. This position serves as a primary point of contact for the office and performs a wide variety of administrative, records management, compliance, and operational support functions with minimal supervision. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Essential Functions: • Serve as a point of contact for Human Resources by greeting visitors, answering incoming phone calls, and responding to inquiries or directing individuals to the appropriate office or staff member for assistance. Provide courteous and professional customer service, particularly when assisting individuals experiencing sensitive or urgent personnel-related matters. • Provide office coordination and administrative support for Human Resources operations, including scheduling meeting rooms, assisting with mail merges, maintaining office supplies, placing food orders, and supporting general office workflow and communications. • Facilitate the completion of employee and student Form I-9 processes by assisting individuals with understanding federal requirements, reviewing documentation, completing employer verification requirements, and ensuring forms are processed and retained accurately in accordance with federal regulations. • Process employment verifications, Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) employment certification requests, address changes, transcript requests, and other employment-related documentation in a timely and accurate manner. • Assist with imaging, scanning, indexing, retrieval, and correction of personnel and employment records within electronic document management systems, including personnel documents, performance evaluations, employment verifications, and new hire documentation. • Assist Talent Acquisition by transferring application materials from the applicant tracking system to personnel files, posting open positions to designated websites, organizing recruitment files for records retention, and supporting other recruitment-related administrative processes. • Maintain and update employee and applicant records within institutional systems, including updates related to certifications, verified credentials, background checks, motor vehicle records (MVR), and other employment compliance requirements. • Assist with Human Resources system maintenance and data cleanup activities, including student employee job terminations in Banner, inactivation of SIAINST records, and PEAEMPL record maintenance. • Prepare and submit required reports and documentation, including the Kansas Department of Labor bi-monthly report and other compliance-related reporting requirements. • Support Human Resources financial and administrative processes, including Concur-related administrative assistance and coordination of departmental documentation and forms. • Assist with maintaining and updating Human Resources forms, webpages, and online information to ensure materials are current, accurate, and appropriately accessible. • Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree or a combination of post-secondary education and additional administrative support experience equivalent to a degree. • Demonstrated effective communication and customer service skills. • Proficient skills in proofreading and using Microsoft Word. • Proven ability to work with colleagues in a team-oriented environment and complete assignments independently. • Ability and willingness to learn and use new computer software. • Proven ability to maintain confidentiality in the workplace. Preferred Qualifications: • At least one year of professional experience working in a Human Resources department. Special Instructions to Applicants: The interview process will require completing a skills assessment to determine candidates’ proficiency in the software and skills needed to perform the position's essential functions. The information will be provided to selected candidates during the interview process. Hourly, Full-time, Mon-Fri, 8am-5pm Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 9b4a7600 Last Name (required) 877cc412 Email (required) 5e2eed06 Job Alert fc6fc25c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Human Resources Human Resources Categories Human Resources/EEO/Title IX Human Resources/EEO/Title IX Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am – 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University’s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 53c00cd6 Last Name (required) 8db9a153 Email (required) 202e6e87 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking “I Accept” or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"
