    "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/retail-specialist-topeka-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Retail Specialist",
      "description": "Retail Specialist - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Retail Specialist Memorial Union Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Retail Specialist Memorial Union Staff Full-time Position Title: Retail Specialist Department: Ichabod Shop Advertised Pay: Base $15.17/hour with potential for a higher entry rate commensurate with experience Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: The Retail Specialist for the Ichabod Shops at Washburn University and Washburn University Institute of Technology campuses provides administrative support to bookstore staff. In addition, the position is responsible for accounting and data entry tasks associated with the maintenance of financial records. As a member of the Ichabod Shop team, the employee must maintain good rapport and extend courteous, honest, and fair treatment to the public, the University community, customers, and co-workers when working the sales floor. The Ichabod Shop represents the bookstores available on the Washburn University and Washburn University Institute of Technology campuses. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Essential Functions: • Count cash on hand and reconcile with money in the safe, daily sales, and daily buyback. Complete and submit daily cash reports to the Director and the Director of Business and Auxiliary Services to keep them informed of sales and their use in further analysis and reporting. • Complete forms and submit cash for deposit following University processes and procedures. • Establish and maintain student charge accounts. Submit Student Charge reports to the Business Office to ensure in-store charges are applied appropriately and timely to student accounts. • Track and maintain daily taxes and Departmental Charges for monthly reconciliation. • Complete and submit payment vouchers to Accounts Payable for accurate and timely payments to vendors. • Work with vendors to ensure Ichabod Shop accounts are in good standing. • Assist the Director with tracking and maintaining Ichabod Shop revenue and expense accounts to ensure accurate financial records. • As assigned, share in opening/closing the Ichabod Shop; provide evening and weekend coverage when needed. (This is usually only once a week.) • Assist with year-end physical inventory counts. • Work with Management and the Finance Office to submit any necessary year-end reports. • Participate in in-store vault audits. Non-Essential Functions: • When needed: assist with ringing up sales, provide cross-departmental support, locate merchandise, and provide information to provide exceptional customer service to customers and exceed sales/service expectations whenever possible. (The need to work the sales floor is not daily.) • Assist with answering phone calls. • During downtime: assist with updating position-related processes, if needed. • Pursue professional growth and development through research, networking, conference and workshop attendance, and other activities. Required Qualifications: • High school diploma, GED, or equivalent. • One year of experience in any of the following areas, individually or a combination of these areas: accounts payable, accounts receivable, collections, payroll, general accounting/bookkeeping. • Six months of retail experience. • Proven effective negotiation and communication skills. • Cash handling skills. Physical Requirements: • Ability to move and maneuver materials weighing up to 50 pounds periodically and up to 40 pounds regularly. Hourly, Full-time Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) d41d8d4c Last Name (required) 5e8cfcfe Email (required) 984dc99c Job Alert 4809e3b5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Memorial Union Memorial Union Categories Retail, Sales, Merchandising Retail, Sales, Merchandising Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am – 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University’s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 4f99f495 Last Name (required) 1f1a3e78 Email (required) 78281404 Refer someone to this job Apply 